  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Tribalco obligated $376M in FY2026 to date across 146 awards. Tribalco's average award size was $2.6M and obligations are up 291.2% year over year. The Department of Homeland Security was the dominant buyer, obligating $347M, followed by the General Services Administration with $16.6M and the Department of Defense with $8M. Radio and Television Broadcasting and Wireless Communications Equipment Manufacturing is the largest NAICS market with $347M, followed by Other Computer Related Services with $15.2M and Surgical Appliance and Supplies Manufacturing with $8M. Historical context shows prior fiscal-year obligations of $146M in FY21, $128M in FY22, $138M in FY23, $87.1M in FY24, and $96.1M in FY25. Current-year totals are partial and represent fiscal year to date figures. This profile highlights concentrated buying by DHS and heavy exposure to broadcasting and wireless equipment manufacturing, with smaller presences in professional services, research, and medical manufacturing markets.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies buy from Tribalco?",
        "body": "The Department of Homeland Security obligated $347M from Tribalco in FY2026 to date. The General Services Administration obligated $16.6M and the Department of Defense obligated $8M. Smaller buyers include the Department of State with $3.8M and the Department of the Interior with $556K."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What are Tribalco's primary markets and award profile?",
        "body": "Radio and Television Broadcasting and Wireless Communications Equipment Manufacturing is Tribalco's largest market at $347M. Other Computer Related Services accounted for $15.2M and Surgical Appliance and Supplies Manufacturing accounted for $8M. Tribalco recorded 146 awards with an average award size of $2.6M."
      }
    ]
  },
